# Column resize handles

Any **left/right column split** (sidebar | main, main | preview, problem | workspace, etc.) MUST expose a horizontal width control via `EdgeResizeHandle` (`axis="x"`).

## Requirements

- Use existing [`EdgeResizeHandle`](src/components/layout/EdgeResizeHandle.tsx) + [`useEdgeResize`](src/hooks/useEdgeResize.ts). Do not invent a second drag API.
- Wrap the sized column in a `position: relative` pane; put the handle on that pane’s shared edge.
- Keep min/max clamps (sensible mins ~200–280px; max from viewport).
- Pane must stay within the viewport: parent `overflow: hidden` / `min-height: 0`; only inner content scrolls.
- Handle on the **left** edge of a right-hand pane → set `invert`.
- Mobile/narrow breakpoints may hide the handle and stack columns; desktop must keep resize.

## Pattern

```tsx
const [sideWidth, setSideWidth] = useState(240);

<div className="split-layout">
  <div className="side-pane" style={{ width: sideWidth }}>
    {/* left column */}
    <EdgeResizeHandle
      axis="x"
      value={sideWidth}
      onChange={setSideWidth}
      min={200}
      max={480}
      label="사이드바 너비 조절"
    />
  </div>
  <div className="main-pane">{/* flex: 1; min-width: 0 */}</div>
</div>
```

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ Fixed grid columns with no handle
<div style={{ display: 'grid', gridTemplateColumns: '240px 1fr' }} />

// ❌ CSS-only resize without EdgeResizeHandle
aside { resize: horizontal; }
```
